# Environment files: where each one lives (2026-10-24).
#
# Three environments, one file each, next to the package that reads it:
#
#                     development              test                     production
#   server/api        .env.development         .env.test                Dokploy (see
#                     (gitignored; copy        (committed, local        .env.production.example)
#                     .env.development.example) values only)
#   apps/web          .env.development         (not needed)             build args from Dokploy
#   apps/app          .env.development         (not needed)             build args from Dokploy
#   apps/mobile       .env.development         (not needed)             EAS / build shell
#
#   development  your laptop's API and apps against the hosted dev services
#   test         the local disposable stack (`pnpm dev:stack`) and the tests
#   production   the deployed stack; its values never live on a laptop
#
# APP_ENV picks the API's file (development | test | production; unset follows
# NODE_ENV). Next and Expo pick theirs from the command (`dev` vs `build`).
# A `.local` file next to any of them overrides it on your machine only.
# Every API variable is explained in server/api/.env.example.
#
#   pnpm api:dev           API on the hosted dev services   (.env.development)
#   pnpm api:dev:test      API on the local stack           (.env.test)
#   pnpm dev:stack         start + migrate + seed the local stack
#   pnpm dev:stack:reset   wipe the local stack and start again
#
# This root file is only for install time: copy it to `.env` (gitignored).

# ── HeroUI Pro (install time) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CI/CD token from https://heroui.pro/dashboard. Required at install time: the
# @heroui-pro/react postinstall downloads the Pro components with it. Without it
# the install passes and every build that imports Pro fails.
# In CI, set it as a secret (GitHub Actions `secrets.HEROUI_AUTH_TOKEN`).
HEROUI_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Optional: personal token for interactive `npx heroui-pro status|login` on your machine.
HEROUI_PERSONAL_TOKEN=

# ── New interface (apps/app, apps/mobile) ────────────────────────────────────
# Embedded database (libSQL/SQLite). Defaults to file:<repo>/.data/injishi.db
# INJISHI_DB_URL=file:./.data/injishi.db

# Allow one-step demo sign-in shortcuts (/api/demo/sign-in). Dev only.
# INJISHI_DEMO_SHORTCUTS=1
